WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.856
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:15.126 --> 00:16.835
Bong.

3
00:16.836 --> 00:19.713
Let us write it in stone.

4
00:19.714 --> 00:23.050
By God's will, we will prosper.

5
00:23.077 --> 00:25.496
We wouldn't have to slave like carabaos [water buffalo].

6
00:26.220 --> 00:28.764
We'll be the ones

7
00:28.765 --> 00:33.269
with workers to till the land for us.

8
00:33.728 --> 00:35.812
Oh, Tino.

9
00:35.813 --> 00:37.147
Wake up!

10
00:37.148 --> 00:39.317
We still have much to harvest.

11
00:39.650 --> 00:41.443
If we don't...

12
00:41.444 --> 00:43.070
they might scold us again.

13
00:43.071 --> 00:46.073
You can talk about your dreams later.

14
00:46.074 --> 00:47.909
The rain is coming.

15
00:49.535 --> 00:51.536
Tell me.

16
00:51.537 --> 00:54.207
Don't you have dreams?

17
00:54.957 --> 00:56.541
Even...

18
00:56.542 --> 00:59.337
to just get out of this town?

19
01:00.088 --> 01:02.964
Do you not want to...

20
01:02.965 --> 01:05.635
grow old with me?

21
01:05.968 --> 01:07.177
Tino.

22
01:07.178 --> 01:10.640
Let us become hacienderos [landowners] here in San Nicolas.

23
01:13.810 --> 01:14.685
Tino.

24
01:14.686 --> 01:17.146
I have a simple dream.

25
01:17.897 --> 01:21.942
I want to build our own restaurant.

26
01:21.943 --> 01:23.902
And...

27
01:23.903 --> 01:28.116
to own land we can farm.

28
01:29.033 --> 01:34.497
And the ingredients we use will come from that land as well.

29
01:38.000 --> 01:40.210
I like that.

30
01:40.211 --> 01:41.628
Alright.

31
01:41.629 --> 01:44.048
Then that is my dream too.

32
01:44.632 --> 01:46.591
You are imitating me.

33
01:46.592 --> 01:47.759
I am.

34
01:47.760 --> 01:51.973
So I can be certain you and I will grow old together.

35
01:56.102 --> 01:57.185
I like that.

36
01:57.186 --> 01:58.770
No, you do not.

37
01:58.771 --> 01:59.730
I like it!

38
01:59.731 --> 02:01.107
Really?

39
02:01.200 --> 02:04.900
"All the Things I Leave You" (Episode 3)

40
02:04.902 --> 02:06.988
Stop here.

41
02:46.152 --> 02:48.987
Here I thought we were gonna do something...

42
02:48.988 --> 02:50.990
Other than this.

43
02:52.200 --> 02:54.034
Why?

44
02:54.035 --> 02:57.163
What were you thinking?

45
03:00.416 --> 03:08.007
Is it true the restaurant won't reopen until Grandpa Tino’s burial?

46
03:08.674 --> 03:10.301
Yes.

47
03:10.801 --> 03:16.098
It's what elders believe around here.

48
03:20.186 --> 03:22.229
Don't worry.

49
03:22.230 --> 03:26.067
You still have a job when the restaurant reopens.

50
03:27.652 --> 03:31.029
How about the other staff?

51
03:31.030 --> 03:34.199
Everybody won’t get paid until you reopen?

52
03:34.200 --> 03:35.533
Just you.

53
03:35.534 --> 03:37.327
You're the only one on probation.

54
03:37.328 --> 03:39.038
Oh, come on.

55
03:46.128 --> 03:48.171
I'm sorry.

56
03:48.172 --> 03:50.757
Grandpa Tino's gone

57
03:50.758 --> 03:54.095
and I'm worrying about other things.

58
03:58.683 --> 04:01.102
I'm sorry too.

59
04:03.729 --> 04:08.818
I don't know what to do now that Grandpa’s gone.

60
04:10.403 --> 04:12.571
His whole life...

61
04:14.865 --> 04:18.493
He was in charge of this restaurant.

62
04:18.494 --> 04:21.289
He was the one we all followed.

63
04:27.211 --> 04:29.504
I think...

64
04:29.505 --> 04:33.383
You'll be our new manager.

65
04:33.384 --> 04:35.136
I know, right?

66
04:36.721 --> 04:38.264
I don't know.

67
04:39.140 --> 04:41.475
I wish.

68
04:42.310 --> 04:43.978
But...

69
04:46.480 --> 04:50.567
I’m sure my family will fight over this.

70
04:50.568 --> 04:52.068
I have to tell you something, Jorge.

71
04:52.069 --> 04:55.489
But don't get mad.

72
04:57.616 --> 05:02.704
Don't you think you're too young to become a manager?

73
05:02.705 --> 05:06.291
Don't you need to finish college first?

74
05:06.292 --> 05:08.293
You know, Kiko...

75
05:08.294 --> 05:12.797
Grandpa Tino didn't have to study to build this restaurant.

76
05:12.798 --> 05:15.968
And he made it grow.

77
05:17.636 --> 05:22.474
You don't need to study to be successful in life.

78
05:22.475 --> 05:25.560
It's because you're rich.

79
05:25.561 --> 05:27.897
For me...

80
05:29.607 --> 05:33.860
It's important to have education.

81
05:33.861 --> 05:38.908
It's more fulfilling to have finished something.

82
06:01.222 --> 06:02.555
So...

83
06:02.556 --> 06:05.434
Should I bring you home?

84
06:26.080 --> 06:28.958
Kiko, can I sleep at your house?

85
06:29.792 --> 06:33.253
I kinda don’t want to see my dad.

86
06:33.254 --> 06:39.050
And our house feels too...

87
06:39.051 --> 06:40.636
Sad?

88
06:41.554 --> 06:43.180
Chaotic.

89
06:45.224 --> 06:46.725
But Jorge...

90
06:48.060 --> 06:50.019
Our house is small.

91
06:50.020 --> 06:52.106
I don’t care if it's small.

92
06:52.648 --> 06:55.609
Size doesn't matter.

93
06:56.026 --> 06:57.528
Huh?

94
06:59.071 --> 06:59.914
Huh?

95
07:00.182 --> 07:01.124
Huh?

96
07:03.075 --> 07:05.035
You don't mind if it’s small?

97
07:08.247 --> 07:10.081
Oh.

98
07:10.082 --> 07:11.958
Actually...

99
07:11.959 --> 07:14.169
Mine isn't that small.

100
07:14.170 --> 07:18.214
But I live in my Aunt’s house now.

101
07:18.215 --> 07:20.384
Oh, I see.

102
07:26.140 --> 07:28.642
I don’t mind.

103
07:32.646 --> 07:34.607
Let's go?

104
07:43.991 --> 07:45.701
Ouch!

105
07:49.371 --> 07:52.082
You weren’t being careful.

106
07:53.167 --> 07:56.169
So, it's my fault now? I'm the one who got hurt.

107
07:56.170 --> 07:58.546
Then what, is it my motorcycle's fault?

108
07:58.547 --> 08:02.426
- Come on! - I can walk!

109
08:07.097 --> 08:08.139
It hurts.

110
08:08.140 --> 08:09.099
Can you do it?

111
08:09.100 --> 08:10.434
Yes.

112
08:21.570 --> 08:23.821
It stings.

113
08:23.822 --> 08:26.158
Still hurts?

114
08:27.034 --> 08:29.661
Manong Kiko?

115
08:29.662 --> 08:31.664
These are my cousins.

116
08:32.998 --> 08:34.708
Jorge.

117
08:35.417 --> 08:36.584
This is...

118
08:36.585 --> 08:37.961
Jasmine

119
08:37.962 --> 08:39.755
and Samantha.

120
08:40.881 --> 08:45.261
Can you get some ice and the first aid kit?

121
08:48.013 --> 08:50.808
They're the ones who wait for me when I come home.

122
08:51.850 --> 08:55.062
They open the door for me.

123
08:57.273 --> 08:58.856
Can I see?

124
08:58.857 --> 09:00.818
Does it still hurt?

125
09:01.443 --> 09:03.028
- Yes. - Jasmine?

126
09:08.450 --> 09:10.076
Thank you.

127
09:10.077 --> 09:13.872
Manong Kiko, is he your boyfriend?

128
09:16.458 --> 09:18.377
Ask him.

129
09:19.420 --> 09:24.215
I can be like an older brother too.

130
09:24.216 --> 09:27.678
Will you also give us chocolates?

131
09:30.681 --> 09:31.890
Yes.

132
09:31.891 --> 09:34.435
Lots and lots of chocolates.

133
09:36.562 --> 09:37.562
Go to sleep.

134
09:37.563 --> 09:40.356
Don't wait for your mom anymore.

135
09:40.357 --> 09:42.860
Go now. It's already late.

136
09:50.784 --> 09:52.786
Does it hurt here?

137
09:54.538 --> 09:57.665
Who gives them chocolates?

138
09:57.666 --> 09:59.335
Oh, that?

139
10:00.169 --> 10:01.920
Don’t mind that.

140
10:05.466 --> 10:07.926
Your helmet's still on.

141
10:09.011 --> 10:09.845
Oh, right.

142
10:09.846 --> 10:11.889
You're crazy.

143
10:16.935 --> 10:18.354
Oh.

144
10:20.773 --> 10:23.608
You have plans to study again.

145
10:23.609 --> 10:25.568
Don't look at that.

146
10:25.569 --> 10:28.322
I happened to see it while passing by.

147
10:29.907 --> 10:31.700
Just like that?

148
10:32.743 --> 10:34.494
I had plans.

149
10:34.495 --> 10:36.788
But...

150
10:36.789 --> 10:40.792
My dad died early.

151
10:40.793 --> 10:43.420
So it was mom who took care of us.

152
10:44.755 --> 10:47.383
But she had a hard time.

153
10:48.342 --> 10:53.638
For now, I'm helping my cousins ‘til they finish high school.

154
10:53.639 --> 10:56.183
Then I'll go back to studying.

155
10:57.184 --> 10:59.936
But they're still so young!

156
10:59.937 --> 11:03.856
Jasmine is still in third grade.

157
11:03.857 --> 11:05.400
Wow.

158
11:05.401 --> 11:12.366
You talk like you finished school yourself.

159
11:21.375 --> 11:25.546
Why didn't you try to apply for scholarships?

160
11:28.424 --> 11:31.468
Who said I didn't try?

161
11:33.470 --> 11:37.432
When I graduated high school,

162
11:37.433 --> 11:40.143
I applied for a scholarship.

163
11:40.144 --> 11:43.897
But I wasn’t so lucky.

164
11:44.398 --> 11:46.692
You know...

165
11:47.860 --> 11:50.696
It hurts to be rejected.

166
11:52.948 --> 11:55.867
I've never been rejected.

167
11:55.868 --> 11:57.327
Okay, wow!

168
11:58.537 --> 12:02.206
Why don't you want to study anymore?

169
12:02.207 --> 12:04.751
How about we study in the same university?

170
12:04.752 --> 12:08.046
You just want to be with me in Manila.

171
12:09.923 --> 12:11.507
That would be good.

172
12:11.508 --> 12:13.384
And...

173
12:13.385 --> 12:16.180
If I run out of money,

174
12:17.264 --> 12:19.767
I can borrow from you.

175
12:22.352 --> 12:24.020
What's in it for me?

176
12:24.021 --> 12:25.396
Well...

177
12:25.397 --> 12:27.315
We'll always be together.

178
12:27.316 --> 12:32.236
And I'll do your assignments.

179
12:32.237 --> 12:34.655
Just that?

180
12:34.656 --> 12:36.783
What else do you want?

181
12:36.784 --> 12:40.077
How about dropping me off at the market?

182
12:40.078 --> 12:41.829
I'll cook.

183
12:41.830 --> 12:43.581
Is that all?

184
12:43.582 --> 12:45.209
Deal.

185
12:48.337 --> 12:51.006
What else did you do?

186
12:52.925 --> 12:55.510
I was a working student.

187
12:55.511 --> 13:01.642
When I was sixteen, I got my driver's license.

188
13:03.644 --> 13:09.775
And I borrowed a motorcycle from Uncle Pilo.

189
13:11.360 --> 13:13.529
Done.

190
13:16.198 --> 13:19.618
How about we go play basketball?

191
13:21.787 --> 13:24.580
What? It's already late.

192
13:24.581 --> 13:27.792
You're forgetting about my burnt leg.

193
13:27.793 --> 13:28.960
You'll do fine.

194
13:28.961 --> 13:31.128
It's cold outside.

195
13:31.129 --> 13:34.382
- Really, now? - That one smells clean.

196
13:34.383 --> 13:36.385
Let’s go!

197
13:43.267 --> 13:45.602
Make sure you can handle me.

198
13:47.771 --> 13:48.938
Looks like you can.

199
13:48.939 --> 13:50.857
Oh.

200
13:50.858 --> 13:52.734
It's locked.

201
13:54.027 --> 13:55.612
Let's go home.

202
13:58.699 --> 14:00.033
Hey!

203
14:00.909 --> 14:02.327
Jorge.

204
14:03.036 --> 14:04.454
What?

205
14:12.462 --> 14:14.297
Forget the gate.

206
14:14.298 --> 14:15.590
Let's climb over.

207
14:15.591 --> 14:18.010
I'll help you. Come on.

208
14:20.262 --> 14:20.721
No.

209
14:20.722 --> 14:22.847
- I'll help you. - No.

210
14:22.848 --> 14:25.725
We’re gonna climb? Over the fence?

211
14:25.726 --> 14:27.018
The patrol will see us.

212
14:27.019 --> 14:28.269
Come on!

213
14:28.270 --> 14:29.813
We won’t get caught.

214
14:31.940 --> 14:33.525
Come on.

215
14:34.151 --> 14:37.487
- I'll lift you up. - I can do it.

216
14:55.213 --> 14:57.007
Told you so.

217
14:58.550 --> 15:00.843
You're acting like you don't want it.

218
15:00.844 --> 15:01.887
Huh?

219
15:03.180 --> 15:05.724
You acted like you didn’t want to climb.

220
15:07.476 --> 15:10.020
- Come on. - Alright, I'm climbing.

221
15:10.646 --> 15:11.855
I can do it.

222
15:14.483 --> 15:16.109
Easy!

223
15:18.779 --> 15:21.156
Here’s the ball.

224
15:27.579 --> 15:30.206
Sir, stop!

225
15:30.207 --> 15:32.250
Kiko!

226
15:33.460 --> 15:35.003
Agnes?

227
15:36.296 --> 15:38.798
I was on my way to your house.

228
15:38.799 --> 15:40.549
I brought you stuff.

229
15:40.550 --> 15:41.884
You just arrived?

230
15:41.885 --> 15:43.302
No.

231
15:43.303 --> 15:45.054
I arrived yesterday.

232
15:45.055 --> 15:47.598
Grandpa made me come home to San Nicolas,

233
15:47.599 --> 15:50.434
so I could fix Grandma's social security.

234
15:50.435 --> 15:52.771
You know, they're getting old.

235
15:53.438 --> 15:54.855
Who's that?

236
15:54.856 --> 15:56.691
- Uh, Jorge. - Jorge.

237
15:56.692 --> 15:59.318
- This is Agnes. - Yes.

238
15:59.319 --> 16:02.947
Agnes, this is Jorge.

239
16:02.948 --> 16:06.076
Hello, I'm Kiko's girlfriend.

240
16:07.953 --> 16:08.829
Uh... she's...

241
16:08.830 --> 16:13.541
Come with me to your house. You can help me carry the stuff I brought.

242
16:13.542 --> 16:15.711
Is your aunt home?

243
16:16.378 --> 16:18.004
Not yet.

244
16:18.005 --> 16:19.422
She'll be home late.

245
16:19.423 --> 16:22.925
Let's go together then.

246
16:22.926 --> 16:25.761
Go ahead. I'm going home too.

247
16:25.762 --> 16:29.932
Invite your friend. He can come with us.

248
16:29.933 --> 16:31.727
No, it's alright.

249
16:32.644 --> 16:34.937
- Let's go, Kiko. - I'm going the other way.

250
16:34.938 --> 16:37.899
Let's go.

251
16:40.485 --> 16:41.862
Ride in the back.

252
17:36.875 --> 17:40.211
Sir, happy anniversary!

253
17:40.212 --> 17:42.714
Happy anniversary!

254
17:44.758 --> 17:45.717
Kiko.

255
17:45.718 --> 17:48.803
You know, in Manila...

256
17:48.804 --> 17:52.681
Our team leader promoted me to a higher position.

257
17:52.682 --> 17:56.769
Now, I have the opportunity to become a team leader too.

258
17:56.770 --> 17:58.479
Things are great in Manila, Kiko.

259
17:58.480 --> 18:02.108
And there are a lot of Ilocanos there.

260
18:02.109 --> 18:06.487
This is good for both of us, Kiko.

261
18:06.488 --> 18:08.781
We're still in a relationship?

262
18:08.782 --> 18:14.371
I promised I would visit every chance I got.

263
18:15.288 --> 18:19.875
And I said that if you choose to work in Manila,

264
18:19.876 --> 18:21.418
then it's over between us.

265
18:21.419 --> 18:24.463
But I never agreed to that, Kiko.

266
18:24.464 --> 18:29.844
Why do you think I keep sending gifts to your aunt and cousins?

267
18:29.845 --> 18:32.806
It's been over for us, Agnes.

268
18:35.809 --> 18:38.227
For you, Kiko.

269
18:38.228 --> 18:40.688
Not for me.

270
18:40.689 --> 18:42.273
Why?

271
18:42.274 --> 18:44.651
Is there somebody else?

272
18:45.986 --> 18:48.445
You chose your job over me.

273
18:48.446 --> 18:50.740
I begged you.

274
18:51.616 --> 18:53.993
Just so you wouldn't leave.

275
18:53.994 --> 18:56.704
I needed to, Kiko.

276
18:56.705 --> 18:58.998
I had to listen to my parents.

277
18:58.999 --> 19:01.792
And that was a job opportunity, Kiko.

278
19:01.793 --> 19:04.420
Do you remember how we couldn't afford places like this?

279
19:04.421 --> 19:07.549
We had no money.

280
19:08.717 --> 19:11.677
But now we do.

281
19:11.678 --> 19:16.348
I'll take care of our expenses while you look for a job, Kiko.

282
19:16.349 --> 19:18.642
I tried my best, Agnes.

283
19:18.643 --> 19:22.647
So I could've provided for you.

284
19:25.567 --> 19:29.361
That's not what I mean, Kiko.

285
19:29.362 --> 19:31.614
What I wanted to say was,

286
19:31.615 --> 19:35.452
Come with me to Manila. Let's start over.

287
19:36.328 --> 19:38.496
Let's start over, Kiko.

288
19:40.874 --> 19:43.210
I don’t want to, Agnes.

289
19:49.966 --> 19:52.636
Is it because of Jorge?

290
19:53.929 --> 19:56.764
There's no one else, Agnes.

291
19:56.765 --> 19:59.225
You left me.

292
19:59.226 --> 20:01.978
We're done.

293
20:42.394 --> 20:44.728
Come here, Kiko. Look at this.

294
20:44.729 --> 20:46.648
Look at what Agnes gave us.

295
20:47.941 --> 20:49.276
Auntie...

296
20:50.026 --> 20:51.611
Put them back.

297
20:52.153 --> 20:55.322
Agnes and I are over, auntie.

298
20:55.323 --> 20:59.994
I don't even know why she's still giving you gifts.

299
20:59.995 --> 21:01.496
Why?

300
21:02.414 --> 21:04.916
Agnes is such a great girl.

301
21:05.792 --> 21:07.584
Look at these.

302
21:07.585 --> 21:10.963
She gave notebooks to your cousins.

303
21:10.964 --> 21:15.927
Auntie, please stop.

304
21:17.470 --> 21:22.516
Can't I decide what's best for me here?

305
21:22.517 --> 21:24.018
Why?

306
21:24.019 --> 21:25.978
What's your plan for yourself?

307
21:25.979 --> 21:28.897
The restaurant closed.

308
21:28.898 --> 21:31.484
What even are these?

309
21:31.901 --> 21:35.322
You’re always searching.

310
21:37.449 --> 21:40.577
Always writing down...

311
21:41.202 --> 21:44.039
But you never send them.

312
22:44.349 --> 22:46.935
- Since when? - What?

313
22:49.854 --> 22:53.440
That you’re falling in love with Kiko?

314
22:53.441 --> 22:56.151
Who said I'm falling for him?

315
22:56.152 --> 22:57.903
You know,

316
22:57.904 --> 23:00.824
This is the part where you're in denial.

317
23:01.449 --> 23:02.658
Take that.

318
23:02.659 --> 23:07.329
Take that pot. Take it.

319
23:07.330 --> 23:09.873
Yes, boss. Wait up. It's heavy.

320
23:09.874 --> 23:12.126
Like your feelings?

321
23:12.127 --> 23:15.547
- Can you stop, Ruth? - Hmm. In denial.

322
23:16.673 --> 23:19.299
Who caught feelings first?

323
23:19.300 --> 23:24.012
If you don't shut up, I'll hit you with this pot.

324
23:24.013 --> 23:24.639
You want that?

325
23:24.640 --> 23:26.975
Hurry over here.

326
23:29.185 --> 23:30.686
Auntie, how many have been made?

327
23:30.687 --> 23:33.397
Eleven ma’am.

328
23:33.398 --> 23:34.607
Eleven.

329
23:35.191 --> 23:36.733
How many days did you make this?

330
23:36.734 --> 23:39.278
Three to four days, ma’am.

331
23:39.279 --> 23:41.531
Three to four days.

332
23:43.616 --> 23:44.826
But...

333
23:46.035 --> 23:48.997
What do you like about him?

334
23:49.497 --> 23:50.747
You know, Ruth.

335
23:50.748 --> 23:52.875
I don't care about him.

336
23:52.876 --> 23:54.835
See?

337
23:54.836 --> 23:57.463
My professor said, that's the next stage.

338
23:57.464 --> 23:59.047
It's called anger.

339
23:59.048 --> 24:02.593
You'll get mad at him. You're angry at him.

340
24:02.594 --> 24:04.762
Take that and put it there.

341
24:05.638 --> 24:08.515
- How many pots were damaged? - Eight, ma'am.

342
24:08.516 --> 24:10.143
Eight.

343
24:12.270 --> 24:14.146
Please take care of it, Auntie.

344
24:14.147 --> 24:18.025
- The pots need to be perfect when we sell them. - Of course, ma'am. I can do it.

345
24:18.026 --> 24:20.737
- Really? - It's easy, ma'am.

346
24:22.572 --> 24:24.699
Okay, Auntie.

347
24:31.998 --> 24:35.667
Oops. That's enough.

348
24:35.668 --> 24:38.921
You're not supposed to be the first to call.

349
24:38.922 --> 24:41.007
Let him make the first move.

350
24:43.426 --> 24:48.096
You learned a lot from your teacher, huh? You know too much.

351
24:48.097 --> 24:50.182
- Look at you. - I know right.

352
24:50.183 --> 24:54.603
My professor even said, "Ruth, you were born to be a psychologist."

353
24:54.604 --> 24:57.022
Mm. See!

354
24:57.023 --> 24:58.524
Okay, okay.

355
24:58.525 --> 25:00.443
I believe you now.

356
25:01.903 --> 25:03.987
What's the next stage?

357
25:03.988 --> 25:05.489
See?

358
25:05.490 --> 25:06.740
Bargaining.

359
25:06.741 --> 25:08.993
You'll start begging.

360
25:10.328 --> 25:12.788
Auntie, why does that have a crack?

361
25:12.789 --> 25:16.833
If there's a mistake, we can fix it so it looks better.

362
25:16.834 --> 25:20.796
How many days will it take to make it?

363
25:20.797 --> 25:23.382
One day, ma'am.

364
25:23.383 --> 25:26.761
- How many have been made already? - Fifty pieces, ma'am.

365
25:28.054 --> 25:30.013
Ruth.

366
25:30.014 --> 25:33.016
What does that mean?

367
25:33.017 --> 25:34.686
Like...

368
25:35.770 --> 25:39.731
You'll do everything just for him to come back.

369
25:39.732 --> 25:41.024
But you know,

370
25:41.025 --> 25:45.779
it's better to confirm if Agnes and Kiko are really a thing.

371
25:45.780 --> 25:51.243
So you have a reason to forget about him.

372
25:51.244 --> 25:54.913
But he's still cute, right?

373
25:54.914 --> 25:58.293
What a wasted opportunity.

374
26:01.087 --> 26:03.297
My god, Ruth.

375
26:03.298 --> 26:06.341
Where is this coming from?

376
26:06.342 --> 26:07.509
Wait.

377
26:07.510 --> 26:09.511
OMG.

378
26:09.512 --> 26:11.805
I have an idea. Hurry up.

379
26:11.806 --> 26:14.349
- What is it? - Take it. Hurry.

380
26:14.350 --> 26:16.268
Hurry up. Carry that.

381
26:16.269 --> 26:19.813
- You know it's hot, right? - Just take it.

382
26:19.814 --> 26:21.565
I have an idea.

383
26:21.566 --> 26:23.026
Wait.

384
26:25.945 --> 26:28.239
Hurry up!

385
26:34.245 --> 26:37.039
How about you help me?

386
26:37.040 --> 26:39.625
What are you going to do with these?

387
26:39.626 --> 26:40.917
I’ll show you.

388
26:40.918 --> 26:42.878
Hold this.

389
26:42.879 --> 26:45.048
- What? - Hold it.

390
26:46.299 --> 26:47.674
Repeat after me.

391
26:47.675 --> 26:49.635
The first one to fall,

392
26:49.636 --> 26:51.345
loses.

393
26:51.346 --> 26:52.889
Say it.

394
26:53.389 --> 26:55.975
The first one to fall, loses.

395
26:56.643 --> 26:57.976
Not like that.

396
26:57.977 --> 26:59.645
Like this.

397
26:59.646 --> 27:01.647
The first one to fall,

398
27:01.648 --> 27:03.566
loses!

399
27:05.860 --> 27:08.737
- That's such a waste. - Those are already damaged.

400
27:08.738 --> 27:10.865
Your turn.

401
27:14.410 --> 27:16.244
The first one to fall,

402
27:16.245 --> 27:18.206
loses!

403
27:21.209 --> 27:22.542
No.

404
27:22.543 --> 27:23.877
Like this.

405
27:23.878 --> 27:26.588
The first one to fall,

406
27:26.589 --> 27:28.633
- Loses. - Wait.

407
27:29.884 --> 27:31.803
Let me.

408
27:35.556 --> 27:37.724
The first one to fall,

409
27:37.725 --> 27:39.143
loses!

410
27:42.397 --> 27:43.855
Just like that.

411
27:43.856 --> 27:45.191
Again.

412
27:46.275 --> 27:47.860
Take it.

413
27:49.237 --> 27:50.529
Together.

414
27:50.530 --> 27:52.072
- The first one to fall, - The first one to fall,

415
27:52.073 --> 27:54.033
- loses! - loses!

416
28:00.206 --> 28:01.456
Good job.

417
28:01.457 --> 28:02.457
Well?

418
28:02.458 --> 28:04.251
Right?

419
28:04.252 --> 28:06.212
I told you.

420
28:12.635 --> 28:15.721
Francisco Cablayan?

421
28:15.722 --> 28:16.681
Ma'am.

422
28:16.682 --> 28:17.764
Scholarship?

423
28:17.765 --> 28:19.434
Yes, ma'am.

424
28:33.114 --> 28:39.536
Friends, the mayor is here. He's arrived. They're here.

425
28:39.537 --> 28:43.373
Insiong, the mayor is here.

426
28:43.374 --> 28:47.377
Of course, that's the mayor.

427
28:47.378 --> 28:48.212
I don’t see him.

428
28:48.213 --> 28:50.422
He’s there, parking the car.

429
28:50.423 --> 28:53.050
Jorge, you have a visitor.

430
28:55.386 --> 28:57.805
Maybe it's Kiko.

431
28:58.806 --> 29:00.307
So what?

432
29:00.308 --> 29:03.226
Jorge, remember what we did.

433
29:03.227 --> 29:04.770
Don't forget.

434
29:04.771 --> 29:07.314
Love is for the weak.

435
29:07.315 --> 29:09.191
The first one to fall...

436
29:09.192 --> 29:10.109
- Loses. - Loses.

437
29:10.110 --> 29:11.110
Yeah, I know.

438
29:11.111 --> 29:13.321
Good.

439
29:26.459 --> 29:31.463
Hey, he's waving at you.

440
29:31.464 --> 29:33.633
He's smiling at you.

441
29:38.721 --> 29:41.140
He's so handsome.
